        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The script has been successfully created and tested. Here's a summary:\n\n**Created `/app/convert_masks.py`** - A Python script that:\n1. Takes 4 required arguments via argparse: `weights_path`, `output_path`, `rgb_path`, `csv_path`\n2. Uses MobileSAM (distilled SAM) to refine all masks from the CSV\n3. Converts rectangular masks to polylines using box prompts\n4. Refines existing polyline masks using their bounding boxes\n5. Resolves overlaps between masks (assigning pixels to smaller masks first)\n6. Ensures each cell has a single contiguous mask\n7. Outputs a CSV with the same structure as input but with updated `xmin`, `ymin`, `xmax`, `ymax`, `coords_x`, `coords_y` columns and all masks as `type: polyline`\n\n**Verification results:**\n- ✅ All 48 masks converted to polylines\n- ✅ Zero overlapping pixels between masks\n- ✅ All masks are contiguous (single connected component)\n- ✅ Output CSV structure matches input exactly\n- ✅ Runs on CPU (no GPU required)\n- ✅ Uses only the specified allowed packages\n- ✅ MobileSAM weights downloaded and working\n\nThe script is ready for use on the hidden test set.",
